          %title
          %p
            %em Comptes rendus hebdomadaires des séances de l’Académie des sciences
            (CRAS) is a journal that published, among other topics, articles in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            (usually under
            = succeed "," do
              %em Algèbre des catégories
            = succeed "," do
              %em Théorie des catégories
            = succeed ")" do
              %em Logique et catégories
          %p
            Currently, it is published under the name
            %em
              %a{:href => "https://comptes-rendus.academie-sciences.fr/mathematique/journals/CRMATH/"} Comptes Rendus. Mathématique
            by the French Academy of Sciences.
          %p The articles are up to 4 pages in length, which means that proofs are usually omitted. While CRAS articles have been archived, their text has not been indexed by search engines, which means it can be difficult to find copies of papers published in the journal. Therefore, here we list various articles pertaining to category theory that were published by CRAS.
          %h2#list_of_category_theory_articles_published_in_cras List of category theory articles published in CRAS
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em> L’obstruction à la construction d’une section d’une fibré au sens de Kan
                , Michel Zisman (1960), (
                %a{:href => "https://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k3202p/f819"}> gallica
                )
            %li
